<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kadashman-Enlil I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned c. 1374–1360 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century-bce">14th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kadashman-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enlil">Enlil</a> I was a Kassite king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a> in the 14th century BCE. Letters in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amarna-archive">Amarna archive</a> record his exchanges with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amenhotep-iii">Amenhotep III</a>, including his sister's marriage to the pharaoh and disputes over gifts of gold and the treatment of Babylonian princesses. He was succeeded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burna-buriash-ii">Burna-Buriash II</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kadashman-enlil-i.jpg" alt="Kadashman-Enlil I" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous (kassite)Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kassite_-_Cylinder_Seal_-_Walters_42619.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
